 - **Talk TM2e-ACTIONS (2026-11-15, TALK round 12; docs/TALK.md 6p):** a reply can do as well as say. Accept an invitation (`TEV_ACT_INVITE`: the resident goes to the venue for the hour through the new `sim_nudge_activity`), a gift from a best friend (`TEV_ACT_GIFT`: `inv_add`), a glutton asks for a food (`TEV_ACT_ASK`: `PROB_WANTS_ITEM`, only without an open problem), call someone over (`TEV_ACT_CALL`: the scene lets them in), walk off. The rule is code and tested: a line says it only if the sim will do it (the plan asks `talk_outcome_can` and the sim first; a spent cap or a minor rule turns the invitation into a refusal with a reason, `TPLAIN_NOYES`), and the sim does it only if the line was said (the event is added with the line, `talk_outcome_apply` does and counts it). Caps: invitation and gift 1 a resident a day and 3 a town day, ask 1. Minor rules in `talk_act.c` with exhaustive tables: no vape shop, concert hall or night beach with a child around, no date, no adult item as a gift or ask, no partner called into a child's room. `TalkLine.action` and the ledger flags cost 0 B (GBA `TalkState` 932 B unchanged). Lines: `act.start` 9, `act.ask_item` 4, `act.call` 6, `hook.gift` 4. 6 new tests (3,000 sessions: every action line has its event and every event was applied). Not in this package: the full census, the ratchet and the lint baseline (the rest of TM2e).
